WEBVTT

00:01:18.210 --> 00:01:25.810
Mike Carter show up yet not yet a diller a dollar a 10 o'clock scholar

00:01:25.810 --> 00:01:29.370
there was an old owl who lived in a note the more he heard the less he spoke

00:01:32.360 --> 00:01:32.960
Yes, Lieutenant?

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:34.650
Mike Carter show up yet?

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:36.080
Not yet, but I think...

00:01:36.080 --> 00:01:37.140
Never mind what you think.

00:01:37.260 --> 00:01:39.060
Just tell him I want to see him the minute he gets in.

00:01:39.450 --> 00:01:40.630
Yes, Lieutenant, I'll tell him.

00:01:41.440 --> 00:01:42.600
What does he want with Carter?

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.980
If I were a mind reader, I'd be making more money.

00:01:45.290 --> 00:01:46.110
Come on, Doris.

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:46.870
What's the inside?

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:50.360
You know Mike and the Lieutenant don't exactly see eye to eye.

00:01:50.480 --> 00:01:51.540
There's no news in that.

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:52.390
Thanks, boys.

00:01:52.470 --> 00:01:53.410
You've been very cooperative.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:54.780
Hiya, Mike.

00:01:55.080 --> 00:01:55.700
Gosh, Mike.

00:01:56.060 --> 00:01:56.940
Mike, how's it going?

00:01:57.100 --> 00:01:57.680
Where have you been?

00:01:57.880 --> 00:01:58.400
What's this?

00:01:58.460 --> 00:01:59.320
You guys been acting up?

00:01:59.480 --> 00:01:59.660
No.

00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:00.720
We've been helping.

00:02:00.880 --> 00:02:01.060
Yeah.

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:01.640
What about that?

00:02:01.820 --> 00:02:02.100
Sure.

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:03.060
It's Sergeant Burr.

00:02:03.140 --> 00:02:04.340
Hey, when are you going to take us to a baseball game again?

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:05.340
Yeah, we got a real team there.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:06.520
We've got to be Boyle Heights last week.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:07.700
Why don't you come down and watch us tomorrow?

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:08.900
I can't make it tomorrow, fellas.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:09.680
Oh, no.

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:10.460
I'll tell you what I'll do, though.

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:11.800
You guys keep your noses clean, and I'll

00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:12.620
take you to the game on Sunday.

00:02:12.820 --> 00:02:13.580
Well, that's our deal.

00:02:13.760 --> 00:02:14.520
Don't forget now.

00:02:14.580 --> 00:02:14.940
So long.

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:15.460
So long.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.040
Make it easy.

00:02:16.460 --> 00:02:16.660
So long.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.580
Hey, speaking of baseball, the A's was won again last night.

00:02:19.860 --> 00:02:20.980
That makes 90, you all me.

00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:21.770
Mike.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:23.410
Unless you want to wait after today's game,

00:02:23.410 --> 00:02:25.140
I mean, even Buck.

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:28.010
You have a lot more to worry about than baseball bets.

00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:29.490
Why, what's up?

00:02:29.570 --> 00:02:29.810
Lieutenant.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.730
Borden's been paging you all morning with warmth.

00:02:33.180 --> 00:02:34.200
What's the beef this time?

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:36.280
Stick around, Kelly. Maybe you can get yourself a headline.

00:02:36.460 --> 00:02:37.760
You wouldn't be planning to kill him.

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.720
Stop reading my daydreams.

00:02:41.860 --> 00:02:42.560
Good morning, Lieutenant.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:45.420
Grapevine tells me you want to see me.

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:46.620
What have I done this time?

00:02:47.460 --> 00:02:49.220
Going off half-cocked as usual,

00:02:50.280 --> 00:02:52.080
using your knuckles instead of your brains.

00:02:53.140 --> 00:02:55.140
Why, what authority did you smash your way into that club

00:02:55.140 --> 00:02:56.340
at 32 Rexford last night?

00:02:56.730 --> 00:02:58.390
I got a tip Fred Portman was in town.

00:02:58.600 --> 00:02:58.960
Portman?

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.580
and got guts enough to show up in this part of the country.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:02.220
I saw him.

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:03.360
I was watching from a close to sleep.

00:03:03.500 --> 00:03:04.300
Well, it looked like him.

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.820
He went in the club, but I never got my hands out.

00:03:05.820 --> 00:03:06.860
Oh, that's great.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.230
It looked like him.

00:03:08.430 --> 00:03:10.630
So you broke your way into the place without a search warrant,

00:03:10.730 --> 00:03:11.990
without authority of any kind of time.

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:14.920
I figured if it was him, we could forget the red tape.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:15.720
Listen, smart guy.

00:03:16.740 --> 00:03:18.600
I'm just as anxious to get Portman as you are.

00:03:19.260 --> 00:03:20.500
It's about time you learn to take orders

00:03:20.500 --> 00:03:21.740
and quit trying to run the whole show.

00:03:22.520 --> 00:03:23.460
Look, I don't get it.

00:03:23.880 --> 00:03:26.120
The Rexford joint's just a phony, a gambling dive,

00:03:26.180 --> 00:03:28.140
a front for every hooter that braces into town.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.280
What's the difference?

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:29.970
No difference.

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:30.860
Not at all.

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:32.840
Except the Vice Squad's been planning a raid

00:03:32.840 --> 00:03:34.840
in that joint for weeks, and you break in and tip him off.

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:36.900
That's great.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.600
Well, I guess I better go in and see the boss.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:42.180
Looks like I got some explaining to do.

00:03:42.320 --> 00:03:43.180
That won't be necessary.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.650
I've already talked to Captain Wayne.

00:03:47.240 --> 00:03:48.180
You don't work here anymore.

00:03:48.760 --> 00:03:49.320
You're suspended.

00:03:49.840 --> 00:03:50.520
Oh, I see.

00:03:50.740 --> 00:03:52.960
And you represented me with the captain, is that it?

00:03:53.580 --> 00:03:53.900
Yeah.

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.370
You talked your way out of things once too often.

00:03:57.330 --> 00:03:58.410
This time, I made sure.

00:03:58.820 --> 00:03:59.960
You've been waiting for a chance like this.

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.480
this for a long time, haven't you, Borden?

00:04:01.940 --> 00:04:03.760
Ever since I first came to work in this department.

00:04:04.260 --> 00:04:05.700
Not a lot of cops like you, Carter.

00:04:06.710 --> 00:04:08.810
You can strong arm your way around town, but not here.

00:04:10.090 --> 00:04:11.710
Now get out of here, you stupid,

00:04:11.810 --> 00:04:13.570
hot-headed flatfoot, before I throw you out.

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:24.690
What's this, Carter?

00:04:25.230 --> 00:04:26.930
Adding in spordination to the rest of your blunders?

00:04:27.160 --> 00:04:28.100
I can explain, sir.

00:04:28.720 --> 00:04:29.960
I think Lieutenant Borden's been pretty

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:31.180
with you from the looks of things.

00:04:31.790 --> 00:04:33.470
Maybe a suspension isn't enough for you.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:35.110
Well, that's all right with me, Captain.

00:04:35.350 --> 00:04:36.310
Let's make it primate.

00:05:25.590 --> 00:05:28.790
Speaking, I'm buying.

00:05:30.520 --> 00:05:32.270
I got all the company I want.

00:05:33.370 --> 00:05:44.120
They tried to reach you to your apartment.

00:05:45.130 --> 00:05:45.810
It's very important.

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:47.590
Keep talking until you say something.

00:05:49.290 --> 00:05:50.670
Did you ever hear of Gene Dyson?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:53.360
Yeah, Continental Meat Packing Corporation.

00:05:54.200 --> 00:05:55.460
I'm a dog lover myself.

00:05:55.820 --> 00:05:58.780
Well, I'm Gene Dyson's nephew.

00:05:59.370 --> 00:05:59.670
Congratulations.

00:06:00.570 --> 00:06:01.630
Mr. Carter, I'm serious.

00:06:02.150 --> 00:06:03.950
Oh, I hate to interrupt your enjoyment of the game,

00:06:04.050 --> 00:06:04.870
but this is an emergency.

00:06:06.420 --> 00:06:09.200
I have reason to believe that Gene's life is in danger.

00:06:10.180 --> 00:06:10.860
Oh, I see.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:12.890
Well, I'm sorry to disappoint you,

00:06:12.970 --> 00:06:14.190
but I'm not with homicide any longer.

00:06:14.350 --> 00:06:14.890
Yes, I know.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:16.610
We heard about that several days ago.

00:06:17.070 --> 00:06:18.330
Say, you get around, don't you?

00:06:18.880 --> 00:06:20.740
Why don't you call up Captain Wayne down at the bureau?

00:06:20.800 --> 00:06:21.560
We don't want to, please.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:25.810
Fact is, Gene's a trifle, well, eccentric.

00:06:26.620 --> 00:06:27.860
Doesn't like publicity and-

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:28.840
Oh, sorry, I'm not interested.

00:06:30.160 --> 00:06:35.460
I, uh, I thought perhaps, uh, $2,000, just as a retainer,

00:06:35.460 --> 00:06:35.840
you understand?

00:06:36.660 --> 00:06:38.680
You'd be employed as sort of a bodyguard.

00:06:39.170 --> 00:06:39.950
$2,000?

00:06:41.170 --> 00:06:43.350
That's kind of a big fee for a bodyguard, isn't it?

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:44.850
I told you, Gene's life is in danger.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.030
Look, get somebody else, will you?

00:06:46.090 --> 00:06:47.710
There's plenty of good private detectives around.

00:06:47.910 --> 00:06:50.260
I'd rather have a man like you, a police detective.

00:06:50.420 --> 00:06:51.440
Say, this guy bothering you?

00:06:51.560 --> 00:06:53.610
No, he's just leaving.

00:06:56.190 --> 00:06:57.290
Carter, you can't refuse it.

00:06:57.430 --> 00:06:58.010
I just have.

00:06:58.230 --> 00:06:59.010
Need any help, Mike?

00:06:59.360 --> 00:06:59.980
I think I can.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:02.450
Goodbye, Mr. Dainey.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:39.280
get it before it gets cold. I'm not much of a bartender, but are you kidding? Nope. Maybe

00:07:39.280 --> 00:07:44.360
it'll help me control my temper. I suppose anybody but you would be pretty disgusted. What makes you

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:50.690
think I'm not? You should be. Well, things are going to be different, though. I'll get myself

00:07:50.690 --> 00:07:58.950
another job. Don't worry, darling. Things get too tough. Why, you can always pawn this. Uh-huh.

00:08:00.120 --> 00:08:01.700
I put it there, and that's where it's going to stay.

00:08:12.370 --> 00:08:13.270
Where are you going, Mike?

00:08:14.040 --> 00:08:14.780
Well, what is it?

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:16.280
Is somebody out there?

00:08:18.420 --> 00:08:19.100
What's the matter?

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:21.480
They're always putting ads or something under the door.

00:08:21.780 --> 00:08:22.760
Does that look like an ad to you?

00:08:23.330 --> 00:08:25.050
No, but it's awfully pretty.

00:08:25.370 --> 00:08:25.630
Yeah.

00:08:26.200 --> 00:08:27.160
Honey, I'm afraid I'm not going to be

00:08:27.160 --> 00:08:29.320
able to take you to the movie, but I'll call you later.

00:08:29.520 --> 00:08:29.960
Where are you going?

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:32.180
High society at the Dyson home in Pasadena.

00:08:32.940 --> 00:08:35.160
I'm gonna give this back and maybe punch some guy in the nose.

00:08:35.460 --> 00:08:37.980
Uh-oh. Temper, temper, temper.

00:08:38.380 --> 00:08:41.100
Now, you know me better than that. I never get into fights.

00:08:43.140 --> 00:08:43.620
Call you later.

00:09:21.310 --> 00:09:23.570
I'd like to speak to Mr. Dyson, Mr. Frederick Dyson.

00:09:24.410 --> 00:09:26.070
He's not in, there's no one at home.

00:09:26.900 --> 00:09:28.240
Just a minute, Dracula.

00:09:28.720 --> 00:09:29.970
If he's not in, I'll wait.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:32.150
Please, sir, you can't come in.

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.170
What do you think?

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:35.510
I've got 2,000 engraved invitations.

00:09:38.710 --> 00:09:39.430
What is it, Peter?

00:09:39.800 --> 00:09:42.320
I'm sorry, Miss Connie, he forced his way in.

00:09:44.580 --> 00:09:47.340
Who are you? What do you want?

00:09:48.810 --> 00:09:49.790
Looking for Fred Dyson.

00:09:49.970 --> 00:09:51.730
I told you, sir, he's not at home.

00:09:51.950 --> 00:09:54.050
What do you mean, smashing your way into people's houses?

00:09:54.250 --> 00:09:57.340
It's all right, Connie. Mr. Carter, I sent for him.

00:09:58.420 --> 00:09:59.500
I felt sure you'd reconsider.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:00.570
Glad you gave.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:04.040
Now look you, I'm returning your bait.

00:10:04.240 --> 00:10:06.320
I don't know which smells fishy,

00:10:06.400 --> 00:10:08.100
are you or this Jarby trying to push at me?

00:10:08.640 --> 00:10:10.400
Anyway, I meant what I said at the ballpark.

00:10:10.860 --> 00:10:11.840
Now lay off, understand?

00:10:12.060 --> 00:10:12.680
Now wait a minute Carter.

00:10:12.940 --> 00:10:14.960
I thought if I could get you to come here, I could explain.

00:10:15.280 --> 00:10:18.920
What is all this noise about?

00:10:19.400 --> 00:10:22.560
I'm sorry Aunt Jean, but I was talking to Mr. Carter here

00:10:22.560 --> 00:10:24.760
about a position and, are you Jean Dyson?

00:10:24.940 --> 00:10:26.980
My aunt owns the continental meat plant.

00:10:27.250 --> 00:10:29.290
Suppose you tell me, Freddie, just what this is all about.

00:10:29.530 --> 00:10:29.730
Well.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:31.700
explaining to Junior here that I'm not for hire.

00:10:31.860 --> 00:10:32.460
For hire?

00:10:32.780 --> 00:10:33.680
I don't understand.

00:10:34.060 --> 00:10:35.140
It's all pretty simple.

00:10:35.720 --> 00:10:36.540
Come in here, please.

00:10:38.770 --> 00:10:39.970
Aunt Gina, I've been worried about you.

00:10:40.090 --> 00:10:41.710
I think you need somebody around for protection.

00:10:41.970 --> 00:10:43.630
You've been trying to tout me into taking a job

00:10:43.630 --> 00:10:44.910
as your personal bodyguard.

00:10:47.170 --> 00:10:47.570
Bodyguard?

00:10:48.820 --> 00:10:50.640
I think he realizes by now I'm not interested.

00:10:51.920 --> 00:10:53.420
Maybe you better keep that in mind, too.

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:56.220
See here, young man, I don't like your attitude

00:10:56.220 --> 00:10:57.790
or your insinuations.

00:10:57.950 --> 00:10:59.970
I certainly don't.

00:11:00.940 --> 00:11:03.670
If I did, I'd choose one with better manners.

00:11:04.200 --> 00:11:06.810
Fine. That makes it unanimous.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:07.740
Just a minute.

00:11:12.960 --> 00:11:14.420
Oh, Connie, you better finish those letters.

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.200
Yes, Miss Dyson.

00:11:22.480 --> 00:11:22.840
Sherry?

00:11:22.980 --> 00:11:25.420
Never touched the stuff, thank you.

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:29.290
About as cozy in here as Grand Central Station.

00:11:31.630 --> 00:11:33.130
What's your first name, Mr. Carter?

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:35.480
Michael C. The C's for Cornelius.

00:11:36.600 --> 00:11:36.900
Why?

00:11:38.280 --> 00:11:41.120
Just wanted to give you a little something for the trouble we've caused you.

00:11:41.670 --> 00:11:43.130
You don't owe me anything. Forget it.

00:11:45.420 --> 00:11:47.640
You're an independent young man, aren't you, Mr. Carter?

00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:50.230
Precisely, what is your objection to working for me?

00:11:50.740 --> 00:11:52.080
I just don't like the way you operate.

00:11:52.670 --> 00:11:55.550
You get a couple of threats, or you tell an unemployed cop to a ballpark?

00:11:56.040 --> 00:11:59.510
Threats? So you told him everything.

00:12:00.156 --> 00:12:02.016
Well, since I hoped to hire him, I felt...

00:12:02.016 --> 00:12:03.876
I told you I didn't want this business talked about.

00:12:03.976 --> 00:12:05.216
It's just some harmless crank.

00:12:05.216 --> 00:12:05.776
But, Angie...

00:12:05.776 --> 00:12:06.636
Nothing to make a fuss over.

00:12:07.324 --> 00:12:09.944
Again, my apologies for your trouble, Mr. Carter.

00:12:10.236 --> 00:12:11.516
Sure you don't want this check?

00:12:12.284 --> 00:12:12.784
Quite sure.

00:12:13.404 --> 00:12:13.764
Good night.

00:12:16.668 --> 00:12:17.748
Take a tip from me, Miss Tyson.

00:12:18.108 --> 00:12:20.108
If these threats are on the level, go to the police.

00:12:20.636 --> 00:12:21.436
That's what they're for.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.300
Incidentally, they're pretty good.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:30.320
That's beautiful.

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:42.810
Nobody fires through that window.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:44.340
All right, Miss Dyson.

00:12:45.920 --> 00:12:47.320
You stay here. I want to talk to you.

00:13:05.240 --> 00:13:06.160
Aren't you going to search the grounds?

00:13:06.340 --> 00:13:07.910
No, whoever did it is gone by now.

00:13:30.188 --> 00:13:30.808
say, will you please?

00:13:37.740 --> 00:13:39.740
Okay, you two can go. Aren't you going to question them?

00:13:39.884 --> 00:13:40.564
I don't have to.

00:13:40.812 --> 00:13:41.852
It was an outside job.

00:13:42.668 --> 00:13:44.548
Apparently whoever did it doesn't know your house very well.

00:13:45.036 --> 00:13:46.636
You see, he aims straight for that mirror.

00:13:47.084 --> 00:13:47.724
But why?

00:13:48.268 --> 00:13:49.728
I'd like to show you something, Miss Dyson.

00:13:50.604 --> 00:13:52.044
Would you mind sitting in that chair for a moment?

00:13:54.604 --> 00:13:56.604
All right, Connie, do as he says.

00:13:57.676 --> 00:13:58.676
Thank you.

00:13:58.764 --> 00:13:59.024
way.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.280
Whoever fired the shots never saw you.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.880
It was your reflection in the mirror.

00:14:15.640 --> 00:14:17.160
He thought you were on the other side of the room.

00:14:19.660 --> 00:14:22.660
It's a very clever deduction, Mr. Carter, but I don't agree with you.

00:14:22.800 --> 00:14:28.140
I'm sure it was just some crank trying to frighten us.

00:14:28.200 --> 00:14:29.640
The mirror was probably a coincidence.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.680
Just the same, Angie, and I still think you ought to let Mr. Carter stay here.

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:34.680
Nonsense. I don't need a bodyguard.

00:14:35.020 --> 00:14:36.380
I think Miss Dyson's right, Freddie.

00:14:36.652 --> 00:14:38.572
It isn't likely there'll be any more danger tonight,

00:14:38.572 --> 00:14:39.992
and you're just upsetting him with all this talk.

00:14:39.992 --> 00:14:40.812
But there's no telling whether or not he'll be back.

00:14:40.812 --> 00:14:42.312
Worrying, Freddy. I'm going to bed.

00:14:42.372 --> 00:14:43.372
You better go, too, Connie.

00:14:46.892 --> 00:14:47.772
I guess that settles it.

00:14:48.556 --> 00:14:49.936
Just don't stand in front of any mirrors.

00:14:50.076 --> 00:14:50.576
Wait a minute, Carter.

00:14:53.228 --> 00:14:55.228
The aunt doesn't realize the danger she's in.

00:14:55.436 --> 00:14:56.996
Please stay, just for tonight anyway.

00:14:57.644 --> 00:14:58.684
She won't even know you're here.

00:15:01.596 --> 00:15:02.596
I'll make it worth your while.

00:15:05.756 --> 00:15:06.536
Okay, Freddy.

00:15:07.196 --> 00:15:08.096
You took me an order.

00:15:56.940 --> 00:15:57.940
What are you talking about?

00:15:57.940 --> 00:15:59.940
The bullets, the ones you just dug out of the wall.

00:16:02.140 --> 00:16:03.280
I was just trying to help.

00:16:03.820 --> 00:16:04.340
Help who?

00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.800
What's that to you?

00:16:06.310 --> 00:16:08.570
I thought Miss Dyson said she didn't need a bodyguard.

00:16:08.790 --> 00:16:09.730
I'm working for Freddy.

00:16:10.550 --> 00:16:12.090
You didn't want me to take this job, did you?

00:16:12.320 --> 00:16:12.640
Why?

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:14.890
It didn't concern me one way or another.

00:16:15.230 --> 00:16:16.490
You weren't too happy about it.

00:16:16.910 --> 00:16:17.610
Should I have been?

00:16:18.600 --> 00:16:20.160
How long have you worked for this outfit?

00:16:20.450 --> 00:16:22.850
Long enough so that I don't have to answer stupid questions

00:16:22.850 --> 00:16:24.050
at 4 o'clock in the morning.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:26.960
I'll miss you.

00:18:34.190 --> 00:18:35.250
I ain't bored in the wet.

00:19:20.600 --> 00:19:22.300
What's the matter, darling? What's happened?

00:19:24.480 --> 00:19:25.240
Borden's been murdered.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:26.800
Borden? Oh, my!

00:19:27.420 --> 00:19:29.510
Yeah, it looks as though I'm the fool guy.

00:19:30.380 --> 00:19:31.480
Well, what are you talking about?

00:19:31.740 --> 00:19:32.980
Whoever did it framed me good.

00:19:33.650 --> 00:19:35.350
Made it look as though I killed him or was on my way

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.850
to dump him when my car got stalled on the railroad track.

00:19:37.970 --> 00:19:39.230
But why? I don't understand.

00:19:40.100 --> 00:19:40.980
Neither do I yet.

00:19:41.840 --> 00:19:43.200
One thing I know, somebody murdered him,

00:19:43.220 --> 00:19:44.340
and I've got to find out who did it.

00:19:44.980 --> 00:19:45.680
You can help me.

00:19:46.100 --> 00:19:47.240
Well, sure. What can I do?

00:19:47.520 --> 00:19:50.140
Well, get down to the office as early as you can.

00:19:50.720 --> 00:19:51.720
Get out Borden's file.

00:19:52.240 --> 00:19:54.020
Every case he's been on for the last couple of years.

00:19:54.600 --> 00:19:55.640
Well, how will I get him to you?

00:19:57.260 --> 00:19:57.700
Let's see.

00:19:58.430 --> 00:19:59.930
Know that I'm using an arcade on 3rd Street?

00:20:00.700 --> 00:20:01.880
Make a record for the folks back home?

00:20:02.040 --> 00:20:02.520
Oh, yeah.

00:20:02.900 --> 00:20:05.300
All right, well, you make a record, or as many as you have to.

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.400
Tell me everything he's done, every case he's been on.

00:20:08.420 --> 00:20:09.220
I'll pick it up later.

00:20:09.800 --> 00:20:10.940
Well, how are you going to get around?

00:20:11.100 --> 00:20:12.740
Your face will be plastered on the front page.

00:20:12.840 --> 00:20:14.100
Not till after the post-mortem.

00:20:14.680 --> 00:20:16.860
That won't be before noon, so I'll have a little time.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:20.790
Now, look, leave the records for Mr. Nolan.

00:20:21.460 --> 00:20:22.460
Right, they'll be there, Mike.

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:23.440
I mean, Mr. Nolan.

00:20:23.560 --> 00:20:24.160
OK, good.

00:20:24.940 --> 00:20:26.500
Now, I'm going down to the Dyson home again

00:20:26.500 --> 00:20:28.020
and play 20 questions with Aunt Jean.

00:20:28.300 --> 00:20:28.860
Oh, wait a minute.

00:20:28.900 --> 00:20:29.540
I'll drive you.

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.820
You'll be much less conspicuous if I'm with you.

00:20:32.420 --> 00:20:34.780
Even a dumb detective like you ought to know that.

00:20:35.810 --> 00:20:36.130
Okay.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:46.760
Okay, honey, get down to the office and get out those files.

00:20:46.980 --> 00:20:48.460
I'll get in touch with you as soon as I can.

00:20:48.920 --> 00:20:50.760
Take care of yourself, Mr. Nolan.

00:20:51.210 --> 00:20:52.430
Don't worry, the Nolans are lucky.

00:20:53.780 --> 00:20:55.770
Oh, Doris, thanks.

00:20:58.440 --> 00:20:59.320
Thank you, Mr. Nolan.

00:21:00.090 --> 00:21:00.490
See you later.

00:21:22.520 --> 00:21:23.340
Eugene Dyson.

00:21:23.670 --> 00:21:24.390
She's not here.

00:21:24.610 --> 00:21:25.990
Well then, let me speak to the butler.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.180
He's not here either.

00:21:27.320 --> 00:21:29.320
Look, this routine's getting a little tired.

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:30.620
Where is Peter?

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:31.820
With Smith Dyson.

00:21:33.190 --> 00:21:34.190
That's where I came in.

00:21:34.370 --> 00:21:38.410
Carter, what are you doing here?

00:21:39.610 --> 00:21:40.630
I work here, remember?

00:21:41.410 --> 00:21:42.110
Yes, of course.

00:21:42.190 --> 00:21:43.570
Then why are you so surprised to see me?

00:21:44.360 --> 00:21:46.690
Not, but I thought you were looking after my aunt.

00:21:47.260 --> 00:21:47.780
Where is she?

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:49.910
I was about to ask you the same question.

00:21:50.530 --> 00:21:51.950
She's probably gone out on business.

00:21:52.070 --> 00:21:53.450
She does occasionally, quite early.

00:21:53.760 --> 00:21:54.580
Yeah, how early?

00:21:54.700 --> 00:21:55.580
4 o'clock in the morning?

00:21:55.780 --> 00:21:56.540
4 o'clock?

00:21:57.390 --> 00:21:58.290
Surely you followed her.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:21:59.980
Yeah, but I sort of lost ..

00:22:00.920 --> 00:22:02.290
I hope she's all right.

00:22:02.990 --> 00:22:04.270
Frankly, Carter, I'm disappointed.

00:22:05.090 --> 00:22:07.330
I expected you to keep an eye on her no matter where she went.

00:22:07.590 --> 00:22:08.070
Don't worry.

00:22:08.170 --> 00:22:09.490
If I don't find her, you'll get a refund.

00:22:10.350 --> 00:22:11.010
Is Connie around?

00:22:11.050 --> 00:22:11.850
I'd like to talk to her.

00:22:11.910 --> 00:22:12.850
I think she's gone marketing.

00:22:13.270 --> 00:22:14.210
She runs the house, you know.

00:22:14.650 --> 00:22:15.810
You trust her, of course.

00:22:17.200 --> 00:22:17.520
Certainly.

00:22:18.320 --> 00:22:19.480
She's very loyal to Jean.

00:22:20.410 --> 00:22:21.450
Okay, I'll see you later.

00:22:21.590 --> 00:22:22.070
Where are you going?

00:22:22.460 --> 00:22:24.280
I've got a few to Taz to check up on.

00:22:25.210 --> 00:22:27.010
Well, incidentally, I'd like to borrow a car.

00:22:27.760 --> 00:22:29.400
Mine won't run so well this morning.

00:22:30.640 --> 00:22:31.860
All right, take the station wagon.

00:22:32.330 --> 00:22:34.280
Thanks. You'll be hearing from me.

00:23:00.700 --> 00:23:01.480
What are you trying to do?

00:23:01.560 --> 00:23:02.300
Get yourself killed?

00:23:02.660 --> 00:23:03.300
What do you want?

00:23:03.440 --> 00:23:04.500
I'm looking for Gene Dyson.

00:23:04.620 --> 00:23:05.300
Where can I find him?

00:23:05.920 --> 00:23:07.600
Oh, Fenton's the one you want to see.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:08.380
He's the foreman.

00:23:09.270 --> 00:23:10.090
Yeah, is that Fenton?

00:23:12.240 --> 00:23:12.560
Yeah.

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:14.430
Looks like he's busy.

00:23:14.800 --> 00:23:15.260
I'll wait.

00:23:18.640 --> 00:23:19.820
Cute little gadget you got here.

00:23:20.080 --> 00:23:20.880
Yeah, very cute.

00:23:21.570 --> 00:23:22.490
Killed a man last year.

00:23:23.220 --> 00:23:24.020
That must have been pretty.

00:23:25.040 --> 00:23:26.220
Yeah, he was a government inspector.

00:23:26.700 --> 00:23:27.880
He slipped and fell against it.

00:23:28.000 --> 00:23:28.160
Kroger.

00:23:28.920 --> 00:23:29.580
Who is this?

00:23:30.700 --> 00:23:31.620
What do you want around here?

00:23:31.700 --> 00:23:33.080
Says he's waiting for Gene Dyson.

00:23:33.920 --> 00:23:34.340
That's right.

00:23:36.010 --> 00:23:36.770
You on the meat business?

00:23:37.620 --> 00:23:39.160
In a way, I keep the meat warm.

00:23:39.990 --> 00:23:40.750
I'm a bodyguard.

00:23:43.050 --> 00:23:43.450
Bodyguard?

00:23:44.130 --> 00:23:44.990
Ask the secretary.

00:23:45.050 --> 00:23:45.930
She'll identify me.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:49.500
OK.

00:23:50.590 --> 00:23:51.110
Wait here.

00:23:51.290 --> 00:23:58.570
What are you doing?

00:23:58.790 --> 00:23:59.530
Making corn beef.

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:02.280
We pump the biome solution into the meat with this.

00:24:03.400 --> 00:24:06.140
And then we cure it by putting in that biome solution that bat over there.

00:24:10.570 --> 00:24:13.170
Good morning, Connie. Still working overtime, I see.

00:24:13.450 --> 00:24:14.370
His name's Carter.

00:24:14.760 --> 00:24:17.040
He says Freddie hired him as night watchman at the house.

00:24:17.590 --> 00:24:20.020
Thanks for the promotion. Is Jean Dyson around?

00:24:20.420 --> 00:24:23.140
Why should she be around? Doesn't she have an office here?

00:24:23.570 --> 00:24:25.210
No, she runs a business from her home.

00:24:25.310 --> 00:24:26.610
You don't have to answer his questions.

00:24:27.940 --> 00:24:28.880
Wasn't she here this morning?

00:24:29.130 --> 00:24:29.970
Look, I told you...

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:41.540
She isn't here now. Why don't you go play bodyguard someplace else so we get back to work? Hey Fenton your slippers showing don't work too hard Connie

00:25:34.890 --> 00:25:35.990
Haven't you got a friend for Harry?

00:25:36.170 --> 00:25:38.650
Gee, that's gonna be sort of tough on such short notice.

00:25:39.420 --> 00:25:41.180
Well, maybe I could get Chlorise.

00:25:41.360 --> 00:25:42.240
Oh, you'll like her.

00:25:42.340 --> 00:25:44.300
She's a neat dancer and a load of laughs.

00:25:44.440 --> 00:25:45.100
Excuse me, miss.

00:25:45.160 --> 00:25:47.120
Did a young lady leave some records here for her, Mr. Nolan?

00:25:47.320 --> 00:25:48.320
I don't know nothing about it.

00:25:48.360 --> 00:25:49.940
If you want some change, I'll give you some change.

00:25:50.040 --> 00:25:52.400
Like I was saying, this Chlorise has a million laughs.

00:25:53.050 --> 00:25:54.250
She's pretty popular, though.

00:25:54.330 --> 00:25:55.290
I ain't sure I can get her.

00:25:55.370 --> 00:25:57.250
Well, my pal, hey, he's pretty popular himself.

00:25:57.590 --> 00:25:59.050
And when he comes to laughs, say he's...

00:25:59.050 --> 00:25:59.970
I hate to bother you, but are you sure you...

00:26:00.000 --> 00:26:00.760
We don't have those records.

00:26:01.060 --> 00:26:02.800
Listen, mister, I told you, I don't know.

00:26:02.920 --> 00:26:04.620
If you want some change, you'll give us some change.

00:26:04.900 --> 00:26:07.300
Say, if Clarissa stayed up, I got another friend, Hazel.

00:26:07.540 --> 00:26:09.120
Look, these records are very important.

00:26:09.320 --> 00:26:10.720
Would you mind looking around behind the counter?

00:26:10.760 --> 00:26:12.080
Now, look, buddy, we don't want no trouble.

00:26:12.260 --> 00:26:13.680
But if you want to make a pest out of yourself,

00:26:13.780 --> 00:26:14.400
you're asking for it.

00:26:14.440 --> 00:26:15.600
Now, take it easy, will you, Sal?

00:26:15.620 --> 00:26:17.500
All I want to do is get these records, that's all.

00:26:17.600 --> 00:26:18.740
OK, Xenia, thanks.

00:26:19.820 --> 00:26:20.380
Wise guy.

00:26:21.740 --> 00:26:22.300
Want something?

00:26:22.520 --> 00:26:24.280
Yeah, have you got any records here for a Mr. Nolan?

00:26:24.770 --> 00:26:25.050
Nolan?

00:26:25.810 --> 00:26:26.970
Oh, yeah, a whole bunch of them.

00:26:29.330 --> 00:26:29.750
Thank you.

00:26:30.000 --> 00:26:31.180
Say, where can I play these?

00:26:31.280 --> 00:26:32.080
Uh, booth's empty.

00:26:32.220 --> 00:26:32.720
Help yourself.

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:33.420
Thanks.

00:26:53.100 --> 00:26:54.720
OK, Mr. Nolan, here we go.

00:26:55.290 --> 00:26:59.970
Beginning with 1946, on January 1, Borden arrested his

00:27:00.000 --> 00:27:05.860
hit run driver Clarence Roebelink, January 3 to 8, routine duty night watch.

00:27:06.300 --> 00:27:11.070
January 9, took charge of Stepniak murder, also Lobo case.

00:27:11.630 --> 00:27:15.570
Stepniak case closed with suicide of killer following gun battle.

00:27:16.130 --> 00:27:19.770
Lobo captured February 6, held for federal authorities.

00:27:20.650 --> 00:27:25.800
February 7 to March 1, Lieutenant Borden in Good Samaritan Hospital for boils.

00:27:26.500 --> 00:27:29.970
Return to duty March 3, assigned with Sergeant Zio-

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:59.870
to Sheldon case, Wilshire district. 22nd to January 8th, 1947, Ferguson

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:05.480
murder, Hollenbeck Heights. Case closed with arrest, conviction, K. H. Thompson.

00:28:06.170 --> 00:28:12.210
January 19, captured Marty Lopez, wanted as material witness in killing of Alberto

00:28:12.210 --> 00:28:18.150
Scarella, a P.E. track walker. I'm not boring you, am I, Mr. Nolan? On January 24,

00:28:18.510 --> 00:28:21.510
another drunk hit-and-runner named Albert T. King.

00:28:31.120 --> 00:28:32.840
June 5, 1947.

00:28:33.360 --> 00:28:36.260
Took charge investigating murder Elysian Park

00:28:36.340 --> 00:28:38.320
involving two gangs of boys.

00:28:38.780 --> 00:28:41.540
Replaced June 12 by Captain McCafferty.

00:28:41.990 --> 00:28:45.790
Sent to Kansas City an extradition case of Otto J. Hamm.

00:28:46.360 --> 00:28:50.510
Returned to LA June 18 and assigned to Night Watch.

00:28:52.310 --> 00:28:55.390
July 5, investigated death of government meat

00:28:55.390 --> 00:28:58.560
inspector Alex Stone at Continental Meat Plant.

00:28:58.940 --> 00:28:59.880
Routine investigation.

00:29:00.190 --> 00:29:07.200
Say doesn't that plant belong to the Dyson family? Yeah, I thought so. Anyway, it rang a bell with me

00:29:07.200 --> 00:29:16.080
I thought I'd give you all the details on July 3 stone the meat inspector fell against hog saw killed him quite dead

00:29:16.300 --> 00:29:21.490
Routine investigation Borden assigned inquest returned verdict

00:29:21.490 --> 00:29:28.850
Accidental death seems stone was nearsighted almost blind didn't tell superiors for fear. He'd be retired

00:29:30.000 --> 00:29:32.360
Borden submitted deposition from I-Man.

00:29:33.000 --> 00:29:36.710
Stone's belongings sent to next of kin, Adam Stone, brother,

00:29:38.460 --> 00:29:40.480
1543 McFadden Street, San Pedro.

00:29:41.420 --> 00:29:44.360
Following this case, Borden took his annual vacation.

00:29:44.930 --> 00:29:47.630
When he came back, Mike Carter was assigned to homicide,

00:29:47.630 --> 00:29:49.150
so you can take it from there.

00:29:49.290 --> 00:29:51.130
And I'm all in.

00:29:51.790 --> 00:29:52.810
Boy, so am I.

00:29:53.520 --> 00:29:54.640
I know you do, honey.

00:29:54.740 --> 00:29:55.980
And I love you, too.

00:31:04.280 --> 00:31:05.840
Take the parkway to Pasadena.

00:31:06.320 --> 00:31:06.500
Right.

00:31:06.760 --> 00:31:08.970
And now for the local headline news.

00:31:09.840 --> 00:31:11.700
Police are turning the town upside down

00:31:11.700 --> 00:31:13.720
in an effort to apprehend ex-detective Lieutenant

00:31:13.720 --> 00:31:16.320
Michael Carter, wanted for the strange killing

00:31:16.320 --> 00:31:17.140
of Lieutenant Borden.

00:31:18.720 --> 00:31:19.520
Fine thing.

00:31:19.700 --> 00:31:21.480
Even the cops are killing each other off nowadays.

00:31:22.430 --> 00:31:22.710
Yeah.

00:31:23.130 --> 00:31:24.490
It's getting tougher every minute.

00:31:25.250 --> 00:31:27.130
Say, can't you get some music on that radio?

00:31:28.050 --> 00:31:28.490
Sure.

00:31:30.030 --> 00:31:43.770
Thanks, he was down at the plant this morning looking for you looking for me. You what are you doing here?

00:31:43.930 --> 00:31:45.550
Don't you know the police are looking for you?

00:31:45.550 --> 00:31:47.250
You think you're gonna get us involved in this mess of yours?

00:31:47.410 --> 00:31:52.850
You're crazy, Freddy. Where have you been since four o'clock this morning? How does that concern you plenty?

00:31:53.480 --> 00:31:56.770
Haven't you told her about our little agreement agreement? What's he talking about?

00:31:56.870 --> 00:31:59.370
I'm sorry aunt Jean, but I was worried about you last night

00:32:00.120 --> 00:32:03.090
I knew you didn't want me to, but I hired him anyway.

00:32:03.430 --> 00:32:03.750
Idiot.

00:32:03.990 --> 00:32:05.910
Couldn't you think of a better way to spend my money?

00:32:06.240 --> 00:32:07.640
I still want to know why you left the house

00:32:07.640 --> 00:32:08.640
at 4 o'clock this morning.

00:32:08.760 --> 00:32:11.600
I always leave at 4 o'clock when I go to the slaughterhouse.

00:32:12.020 --> 00:32:13.400
Not that it's any of your business.

00:32:13.640 --> 00:32:15.700
You aren't headed for any slaughterhouse when I followed you.

00:32:16.020 --> 00:32:16.840
You followed me?

00:32:16.960 --> 00:32:18.980
Yeah, to the warehouse district in downtown LA.

00:32:19.330 --> 00:32:19.850
Of course.

00:32:20.170 --> 00:32:22.030
That's where I pick up Wilson, my buyer.

00:32:22.430 --> 00:32:22.750
Really?

00:32:23.380 --> 00:32:25.840
Isn't it a little unusual for a woman to go to a slaughterhouse

00:32:25.840 --> 00:32:26.420
at that hour?

00:32:26.560 --> 00:32:27.140
Not at all.

00:32:27.560 --> 00:32:29.900
The head of our company has always personally selected

00:32:30.000 --> 00:32:34.410
the meat. That's why the Dyson Company has stayed on top all these years. I used to go

00:32:34.410 --> 00:32:37.350
with my father when I was a girl and I've carried on ever since his death.

00:32:38.260 --> 00:32:41.520
All right, I'll buy that for the moment. Now that you know all about my aunt, will you

00:32:41.520 --> 00:32:48.700
please leave or shall we call the police? No, Freddie, wait. Well, this is real

00:32:48.700 --> 00:32:53.180
touching. Why so considerate of a murder suspect? You know how Miss Dyson

00:32:53.180 --> 00:32:56.320
feels about notoriety and you have no right to get her mixed up in your

00:32:56.320 --> 00:32:56.620
Affairs.

00:33:00.060 --> 00:33:02.840
A meat inspector was killed last year at your sausage factory.

00:33:03.000 --> 00:33:04.860
What about it? What's that got to do with you?

00:33:05.720 --> 00:33:06.860
I'm not too sure yet.

00:33:07.020 --> 00:33:09.560
The man got killed, that's all. The inquest proved it was an accident.

00:33:10.020 --> 00:33:12.500
He had bad eyes, but wouldn't tell anyone for fear he'd lose his job.

00:33:20.680 --> 00:33:21.240
Police department.

00:33:21.420 --> 00:33:22.680
No, you can't. Not from here.

00:33:24.550 --> 00:33:25.250
Police department.

00:33:26.340 --> 00:33:27.040
Ask for homicide.

00:33:27.280 --> 00:33:27.840
I will not.

00:33:28.020 --> 00:33:29.700
Do as I tell you. You want me to get out of here, don't you?

00:33:32.010 --> 00:33:46.340
extension 229 give me homicide please extension 229 hello this is mr. Nolan

00:33:47.000 --> 00:33:54.260
arcade drapery company oh oh yes what is it remember that material that seemed

00:33:54.700 --> 00:33:59.800
to ring a bell with you a little more detail if possible oh yes I I know

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:07.550
What you mean, but I couldn't possibly get away till after five. Well, that's fine. I'll bring the material to

00:34:08.700 --> 00:34:14.740
Adam's place. You'll find the address with the material. Good. Thank you so much

00:34:15.240 --> 00:34:19.980
What was that all about? Oh, I'm just gonna run up a set of drapes for an old friend of mine

00:34:19.980 --> 00:34:21.980
And now there's nothing more mr. Carter. No more telephone

00:34:21.980 --> 00:34:27.690
All right, Freddy. I'm leaving by the way if you want your station wagon, you'll find it on third street. You can't miss it

00:34:28.290 --> 00:34:29.970
It's parked right next to a fire hydrant

00:35:24.960 --> 00:35:29.860
something? Yes, I'm looking for Adam Stone. That's me. Mind if I ask you a couple of questions? Sure.

00:35:30.000 --> 00:35:32.600
What's your trouble? I can fix anything from a yacht to a rowboat.

00:35:32.680 --> 00:35:33.440
I bet you could.

00:35:33.980 --> 00:35:35.320
That's not what I want to ask you about, though.

00:35:36.170 --> 00:35:36.950
It's about your brother, Alex.

00:35:38.980 --> 00:35:39.620
What about Alex?

00:35:40.730 --> 00:35:41.750
Well, you see, I'm from the police.

00:35:42.400 --> 00:35:43.780
Oh, what do you want to know?

00:35:43.940 --> 00:35:46.990
I imagine Lieutenant Borden has already contacted you.

00:35:47.380 --> 00:35:47.660
Borden?

00:35:47.940 --> 00:35:50.710
No. Who's he?

00:35:51.540 --> 00:35:52.920
You mean you never heard of Lieutenant Borden?

00:35:53.560 --> 00:35:54.360
Can't say I have.

00:35:55.490 --> 00:35:56.670
He was in charge of the investigation

00:35:56.670 --> 00:35:57.830
at the time of your brother's death.

00:35:58.080 --> 00:35:59.800
A policeman was here, but I don't know that he was a lieutenant.

00:36:00.000 --> 00:36:10.440
He brought me Alex belongings. I say you still have them in the back room mind if I take a look at them from this way

00:36:10.440 --> 00:36:20.070
Right here just a suitcase with some of these things. Actually, I want to keep them

00:36:31.760 --> 00:36:32.600
He didn't leave much.

00:36:33.130 --> 00:36:34.970
A couple of suits I gave to the Salvation Army.

00:36:36.300 --> 00:36:37.720
Boy, he didn't leave much is right.

00:36:39.100 --> 00:36:39.580
What's this?

00:36:39.860 --> 00:36:41.640
That's the way he killed time, hobby of my color.

00:36:43.540 --> 00:36:44.500
These were his tools.

00:36:45.760 --> 00:36:46.540
Very delicate work.

00:36:47.380 --> 00:36:47.980
Sure is.

00:36:48.570 --> 00:36:49.350
You see that poor Rigger?

00:36:49.570 --> 00:36:51.760
He gave that to me a couple of years ago.

00:36:52.680 --> 00:36:53.500
Wonderful out of detail.

00:36:54.590 --> 00:36:55.210
Nice job.

00:36:56.210 --> 00:36:58.070
Must have been working on this one time he got killed.

00:36:59.120 --> 00:36:59.800
Never got it finished.

00:37:01.020 --> 00:37:02.860
He wasn't social, what you call a mixer.

00:37:03.890 --> 00:37:07.080
He spent most of his spare time making these boats.

00:37:10.350 --> 00:37:13.430
Well, once obliged, thanks very much for your trouble.

00:37:13.610 --> 00:37:14.070
That's all right.

00:37:14.270 --> 00:37:14.570
So long.

00:37:24.200 --> 00:37:25.840
Operator, give me the police.

00:37:39.320 --> 00:37:40.420
Sure nobody tells you.

00:37:40.560 --> 00:37:41.140
I don't think so.

00:37:41.340 --> 00:37:42.140
Listen, you're on.

00:37:43.180 --> 00:37:44.540
According to the latest bulletin,

00:37:44.800 --> 00:37:47.640
Mike Carter wanted in connection with the murder of Lieutenant Borden.

00:37:48.040 --> 00:37:50.400
Seen early today in the vicinity of East Third Street.

00:37:51.360 --> 00:37:54.400
Joe Torque, cab driver, reported driving him to Pasadena.

00:37:55.400 --> 00:37:57.400
You have to hand it to those guys down at Homicide.

00:37:57.580 --> 00:37:58.360
Right on the job.

00:38:00.000 --> 00:38:02.200
Had a little trouble getting it.

00:38:06.880 --> 00:38:11.640
See, July 5, Borden, Stone, Hogsore, continental meet.

00:38:12.880 --> 00:38:14.060
Verdict, accidental death.

00:38:15.700 --> 00:38:17.020
Nearsighted, submitted deposition.

00:38:18.010 --> 00:38:19.190
Adam Stone, San Pedro.

00:38:20.640 --> 00:38:21.680
An annual vacation.

00:38:22.740 --> 00:38:23.360
That's all, huh?

00:38:23.770 --> 00:38:24.750
That's all there was.

00:38:25.270 --> 00:38:27.250
And if they find out, I walked off with it.

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:29.800
Brother will be in the same boat.

00:38:30.380 --> 00:38:31.680
Oh, don't worry, honey, you'll get it back.

00:38:32.980 --> 00:38:35.630
Boat. Wait a minute, that's it, the boat.

00:38:36.530 --> 00:38:37.070
What boat?

00:38:37.660 --> 00:38:38.980
The half-finished one on the bottle.

00:38:39.760 --> 00:38:42.320
Haven't you noticed everybody connected with this case goes out of his way?

00:38:42.520 --> 00:38:44.920
Leans over backwards to emphasize this guy's weak eyes.

00:38:45.520 --> 00:38:46.520
Look at all these reports.

00:38:47.070 --> 00:38:49.250
They even went to the trouble of getting a statement from an eye man.

00:38:49.950 --> 00:38:50.230
So?

00:38:51.050 --> 00:38:54.200
I just got a load of the guy's hobby, carving ships and bottles.

00:38:54.920 --> 00:38:56.040
It's the trickiest kind of work.

00:38:56.140 --> 00:38:57.740
Why, it must take perfect eyes.

00:38:58.260 --> 00:38:59.920
Well, maybe he did it before his eyes went back.

00:39:00.620 --> 00:39:03.390
This one was only half-finished. He was working on it when he was killed.

00:39:04.610 --> 00:39:08.490
Then somebody must have been awfully anxious to make that coroner's verdict read accidental.

00:39:09.250 --> 00:39:14.500
Yeah. Honey, we're going to 4024 South Figueroa to see this guy Breller.

00:39:56.400 --> 00:39:59.860
I do for you I some bad headaches lately I thought maybe I need

00:40:00.060 --> 00:40:02.660
Come into the examining room.

00:40:10.330 --> 00:40:10.730
Sit down.

00:40:11.520 --> 00:40:11.700
Over there.

00:40:11.820 --> 00:40:16.920
Put your head back.

00:40:17.300 --> 00:40:17.580
Relax.

00:40:20.420 --> 00:40:20.920
Look up here.

00:40:21.060 --> 00:40:24.240
One of mine recommended you.

00:40:24.500 --> 00:40:25.460
Gave you quite a build up.

00:40:26.950 --> 00:40:27.130
Yeah?

00:40:30.600 --> 00:40:34.800
Too bad about Alex, wasn't it?

00:40:37.170 --> 00:40:37.370
Yeah.

00:40:39.760 --> 00:40:41.380
Just how bad would you say his eyes were?

00:40:49.940 --> 00:40:51.340
Try and read the bottom line on that chart.

00:40:53.950 --> 00:40:59.940
A, P, E, O, X.

00:41:00.640 --> 00:41:01.580
Y-Z.

00:41:01.920 --> 00:41:11.370
What happened?

00:41:11.530 --> 00:41:11.910
Any luck?

00:41:11.990 --> 00:41:12.670
It choked me.

00:41:13.460 --> 00:41:14.820
No, the prescription isn't there.

00:41:15.310 --> 00:41:15.870
How about it, Doc?

00:41:16.240 --> 00:41:17.820
Where's the prescription for Alex Stone's glasses?

00:41:18.780 --> 00:41:19.860
He's been dead a year.

00:41:19.980 --> 00:41:21.380
I don't hang on to those things forever.

00:41:21.620 --> 00:41:22.720
Yeah, well, who's behind all this?

00:41:22.840 --> 00:41:24.360
Who's this mug that's trying to sap me?

00:41:24.460 --> 00:41:25.620
He's a patient of mine.

00:41:26.450 --> 00:41:27.850
Recognizing you wanted some murder.

00:41:28.130 --> 00:41:28.450
Yeah?

00:41:28.810 --> 00:41:29.910
Who told you I'd be coming here?

00:41:30.250 --> 00:41:31.170
Who told you I said?

00:41:31.410 --> 00:41:32.550
Okay, let me breathe.

00:41:32.830 --> 00:41:33.410
All right.

00:41:34.620 --> 00:41:38.650
Ooh! Get out of here fast.

00:41:46.280 --> 00:41:48.560
Anybody here? I got something in my eye.

00:41:58.130 --> 00:41:59.110
Down over here, please.

00:41:59.770 --> 00:41:59.970
The doctor...

00:42:00.000 --> 00:42:01.240
The doctor will be just a few minutes.

00:42:01.400 --> 00:42:03.100
The best thing to do is lean your head back

00:42:03.100 --> 00:42:04.340
and keep your eyes closed.

00:42:05.020 --> 00:42:06.460
There, it won't be very long.

00:42:16.220 --> 00:42:18.460
You'd better hold that towel so that it doesn't fall off.

00:42:18.600 --> 00:42:20.080
The doctor will just be a few minutes.

00:42:20.280 --> 00:42:20.640
Yes, ma'am.

00:42:24.780 --> 00:42:26.240
Why, how do you do, Mrs. Heffelmeyer?

00:42:26.360 --> 00:42:27.160
So glad to see you.

00:42:27.260 --> 00:42:28.560
The doctor will just be a few minutes.

00:42:28.680 --> 00:42:29.640
Come in and sit down, please.

00:42:31.280 --> 00:42:58.630
Clear. Black sedan. No license. Code three. Number 61. Clear. Number four. Call in. Robert. Check your spare. All units. Mike Carter reported in vicinity of San Pedro. All units. San Pedro. Number 61. Clear. Number 18. Clear.

